</nav>

<main class="page">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Owner Operator Proof Pack</span>
      <h1>How Seascape protects what an owner actually keeps.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">The <a href="/research/owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026/">owner benchmark</a> shows why the management fee is only part of the comparison. This page shows the next question: what Seascape has already seen, protected, or made clearer in real operating examples.</p>
      <p class="hero-lead">Use it before you request the private teardown. The examples are redacted, narrow, and labeled so they do not pretend one property proves every property.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/property-management/?owner_source=how-seascape-protects-owner-net-2026#owner-cta" data-track-event="owner_primary_cta_click" data-page-slug="how-seascape-protects-owner-net-2026">Request Your Revenue Teardown</a>
        <a class="btn btn-light" href="#proof-modules">See proof modules</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-panel">
      <span class="eyebrow">What this page proves</span>
      <h2>Execution proof, not another fee explainer.</h2>
      <ul class="proof-list">
        <li><strong>{{ proofPack.modules.length }} proof modules</strong><span>Redacted operating examples from the current Hub proof library.</span></li>
        <li><strong>{{ proofPack.lastRefreshedLabel }}</strong><span>Current reuse window runs through {{ proofPack.staleAfter }} unless newer owner-report proof replaces it.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Same teardown path</strong><span>The next step stays the property-specific review, with source attribution preserved.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="source-note">
    <p><strong>Source note:</strong> {{ proofPack.sourceLabel }} backed by {{ proofPack.sourcePath }}. {{ proofPack.redactionNote }} {{ proofPack.demandBoundary }}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="proof-modules">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <span class="eyebrow">Operating examples</span>
        <h2>Four examples that answer what Seascape can actually show you.</h2>
        <p>Each module says what changed, why it mattered, and what the example still cannot prove. That keeps the page useful without turning redacted owner material into a public guarantee.</p>
        <div class="proof-chip-row">
          <span class="proof-chip">Redacted summaries</span>
          <span class="proof-chip">Last refreshed: {{ proofPack.lastRefreshedLabel }}</span>
          <span class="proof-chip">5-property Gulf Coast scope</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="module-grid">
        {% for item in proofPack.modules %}
        <article class="module-card">
          <div class="module-meta">
            <span class="module-type">{{ item.type }}</span>
            <span class="module-label">{{ item.proofLabel }}</span>
          </div>
          <h3>{{ item.headline }}</h3>
          <div class="metric-pair">
            <div class="metric-box">
              <strong>{{ item.metric }}</strong>
              <span>{{ item.metricLabel }}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="metric-box">
              <strong>{{ item.supportingMetric }}</strong>
              <span>{{ item.supportingLabel }}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p><strong>What changed:</strong> {{ item.whatChanged }}</p>
          <p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> {{ item.whyItMatters }}</p>
          <p class="boundary"><strong>Boundary:</strong> {{ item.boundary }}</p>
          <span class="evidence-path">Evidence path: {{ item.evidencePath }}</span>
        </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container bridge-grid">
      <div class="bridge-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">How this fits the benchmark</span>
        <h3>First understand the math. Then ask whether the operator can prove the work.</h3>
        <p>The <a href="/research/owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026/">Owner Fee + Revenue Benchmark</a> explains management fee, Airbnb cost, direct payment cost, and example math. This proof pack sits one step later: it shows how Seascape reports and explains those issues when they appear in actual owner material.</p>
        <ul class="plain-list">
          <li>Booking-source cost should be visible, not buried inside occupancy.</li>
          <li>Direct bookings should be named as real wins without pretending they solve every channel problem.</li>
          <li>Owner reports should end with the next decision, not a pile of unexplained activity.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="boundary-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">What stays private</span>
        <h3>The public page does not replace your teardown.</h3>
        <div class="boundary-table">
          <div class="boundary-row"><strong>Public proof</strong><span>Redacted operating examples and benchmark facts already visible on the site.</span></div>
          <div class="boundary-row"><strong>Private teardown</strong><span>Your listing URL, statement, fee quote, calendar, reviews, and manager context.</span></div>
          <div class="boundary-row"><strong>Unknowns</strong><span>Missing statements, reviews, calendars, or fee terms get marked missing instead of guessed.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-shell" id="owner-cta">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro section-intro--center">
        <span class="eyebrow">Private teardown</span>
        <h2>Want this same review for your home?</h2>
        <p>Send the easiest proof you have. A listing URL is enough to start; an owner statement or fee quote makes the review sharper.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-card">
        <div class="cta-grid">
          <div class="cta-copy">
            <h3>Request a Revenue Teardown</h3>
            <p>Seascape will separate what is proven, what is likely, and what is still missing before recommending whether to stay put, fix the current setup, or talk about transition.</p>
            <p class="cta-proof-note">This is the same teardown path used by the owner hub. The source is tracked as this proof pack so the route can be measured separately.</p>
          </div>
          {{ ownerEvaluationForm({
            className: "owner-lead-form--benchmark",
            formPlacement: "operator-proof-pack-teardown",
            pageSlug: "how-seascape-protects-owner-net-2026",
            sourcePageSlug: "how-seascape-protects-owner-net-2026",
            market: "florida-gulf-coast",
            leadType: "owner-revenue-teardown",
            buttonLabel: "Send My Teardown Request",
            propertyFieldLabel: "Property address or market",
            propertyFieldPlaceholder: "Market or street address",
            showBenchmarkFields: true,
            allowFileUpload: true,
            suppressNote: true,
            gridClassName: "owner-form-grid--benchmark",
            fileHelp: "PDF, spreadsheet, or screenshot. Missing statements, calendars, reviews, or fee terms will be marked as missing."
          }) }}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="footer">© 2026 <a href="/">Seascape Vacations</a> · <a href="/property-management/">Property Management</a> · <a href="/research/owner-fee-revenue-leak-benchmark-2026/">Owner Benchmark</a></footer>
</body>
</html>
